---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "@/components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import Main from "@/components/Main.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import config from "@/config";
---

<Layout
  title={`Editorial Process | ${config.site.title}`}
  description="How The Smart Suburbanite researches, reviews, updates, and corrects its practical smart-home guides."
>
  <Header />
  <Breadcrumb />
  <Main pageTitle="Editorial Process" class="app-prose trust-page">
    <p class="page-intro">
      The Smart Suburbanite is an independently operated publication. Its goal
      is to help readers make calmer, better-informed smart-home decisions with
      research-based guidance and clear limits.
    </p>

    <h2>What we publish</h2>
    <p>
      The site publishes practical guidance about compatibility and setup,
      subscription and maintenance trade-offs, privacy and household access, and
      product-neutral decision support. A guide should help answer a real
      homeowner question, not simply repeat a product feature list.
    </p>

    <h2>How topics are selected</h2>
    <p>
      Topics begin with a concrete reader problem and must offer a useful
      decision, comparison, checklist, or explanation. Vague trend summaries,
      unsupported product rankings, and subjects that cannot be handled with
      appropriate evidence are avoided.
    </p>

    <h2>Source hierarchy</h2>
    <p>Research generally gives preference to sources in this order:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Official manufacturer support and product documentation.</li>
      <li>Government, regulatory, standards, and public-interest sources.</li>
      <li>Established technical or consumer references.</li>
      <li>Reputable secondary reporting used for context.</li>
      <li>
        Lower-authority sources only when necessary and clearly identified.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Product plans, subscriptions, compatibility, support policies, and app
      behavior can change. Date-sensitive details are checked near publication
      and should be confirmed again before a critical purchase or installation
      decision.
    </p>

    <h2>Research-based and tested content</h2>
    <p>
      Most guides are based on published documentation and editorial research.
      The site does not claim hands-on testing unless that testing actually
      occurred and is disclosed. Manufacturer descriptions are treated as
      product documentation, not independent proof. Guides do not guarantee
      compatibility, savings, safety, privacy, or performance.
    </p>

    <h2>AI assistance</h2>
    <p>
      AI tools may assist with outlining, drafting, comparison structure,
      wording, editing, or quality checks. AI output is not published without
      human review. The human operator reviews factual claims, wording limits,
      uncertainty, revisions, and the final publication decision. Fabricated
      product use, interviews, personal experiences, and credentials are
      prohibited.
    </p>

    <h2>Human review</h2>
    <p>The human operator reviews:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the reader question and the article promise;</li>
      <li>important claims and the quality of supporting sources;</li>
      <li>uncertainty, limitations, and misleading certainty;</li>
      <li>unsupported personal experience or product-testing language; and</li>
      <li>the final revision and publication decision.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Readers may report errors through the <a href="/contact/"
        >public contact method</a
      >. Substantive factual corrections are reviewed against current sources.
      Modification dates are shown where the publishing system supports them. A
      request does not guarantee a change when the evidence does not support
      one.
    </p>

    <h2>Updates</h2>
    <p>
      Articles may be updated when material plan, subscription, compatibility,
      support, or product-policy details change. Readers should confirm critical
      purchase and installation details with current manufacturer documentation.
    </p>

    <h2>Commercial independence</h2>
    <p>
      At the time of this update, The Smart Suburbanite has no affiliate links,
      sponsored placements, paid product rankings, paid product placements, or
      display ads. Future commercial relationships will be disclosed clearly if
      they are introduced.
    </p>
  </Main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
